n there's something  wrong with us not the plan we're told  that we're responsible for everybody  else's feelings and that our goal in  relationships is to be right and to get  things from each other not to just be  with one another we don't know how to be  married anymore  we don't know how to have kids anymore  we don't know how to deal with  technology in our lives and our houses  are on fire and so when I say examine  your ecosystem sit down with yourself  sit down with your partner sit down with  your kids if they're old enough and  paint a picture of what you want this to  look like what do you want your life to  look like not where do you want to be in  five years  and what title do you want to have and  what amount of money do you want to make  because here's what sucks about living  that life no matter what job you get you  go with you no matter how much money you  have in your bank account you're the one  that has to go deposit that money the  worst part about getting a new  girlfriend a new boyfriend a new husband  is that you go with you if you don't do  the hard work of identifying the  ecosystem that you want to create you're  never gonna be whole it's time to take  inventory of your life it's time to look  around at your ecosystem what are things  you need to say no to what are  boundaries you need to put up what are  relationships that you need to fix  because you're doing things that aren't  helpful  what are new books you need to read what  are new people you need to connect with  examine the ecosystem of your life  number two I talked about this in the  last video and I'm gonna expand on it  here we've got to take care of our  hearts our minds our souls and our  bodies chronic stress is killing us it  is killing us this isn't a game it's not  a game mindfulness prayer belief in God  those aren't funny things that we used  to do long ago and now suddenly we've  got iPhones in sophistication and we  don't need to honor our hearts and our  minds anymore wrong you have to submit  to something bigger than you I'm a  Christian guy so I buy into a Christian  God you've got to meditate you've got to  pray those are non negotiables for a  healthy stress-free alarm free life  you've got to exercise pull up the  Internet's there's a thousand different  workouts most professionals that I talk  to now when I ask them what's the best  workout you can do they say anyone that  you will stick with  yoga heavy lifting running I don't care  do what works for you but you got to do  something you got to take care of your  mind  I know tiger King was fun but a good  book would have been better I know just  scrolling through Netflix and spending  mindless hours on different apps and  scrolling machine thingies feels good  it's a distraction but it doesn't feed  our minds to give your mind your body  your spirit your soul take care of  yourself number three invest in new and  existing relationships as I talked about  in the last video we cannot do life  alone we can't and that means we have to  learn how to do things like say I'm  sorry I screwed it up I shouldn't have  been texting her I shouldn't have called  him I need to be a better dad and I'm  sorry learning how to say I need help  my alarms are spinning I can't pick up  this couch by myself my wife is sad and  it's my fault and I don't know what to  do  learning to look somebody in the eye and  say I love you and I haven't done it  right all the time but I love you I  don't want to get this right  finding people to invest in to loved  over the long term one of my mentors dr.  Richard Beck asked a question that still  haunts me  he said what if we lived our lives as  that we would never move what  conversations would we have with our  neighbors our church members our friends  what ways would we treat people when we  messed up instead of running away  finding a new church home moving to a  new house taking a new job what if we  worked hard on the relationship that we  have what if we took care of our loved  ones and we said I'm sorry I'm gonna do  better next time  number four when you need it get  professional help I've seen a counselor  I've seen a medical doctor there was a  season I was on medication I've worked  with all different kinds of people from  single moms with three kids to  multimillionaires who are all struggling  with the same anxiety alarms nobody's  immune and there's moments in time when  we have to submit and Saturday December  national help get the help you need you  are worth it if you've got somebody in  your life that needs help encourage them  to get the professional help that they  need so a quick recap examine your  ecosystem and take an inventory of your  life your relationships and the things  you think you want to do number two take  care of your mind your body your spirit  your soul number three take care of and  invest in new relationships we cannot do  this alone  number four when necessary get  professional help don't be ashamed to go  see a counselor don't be ashamed to go  visit with your pastor don't be ashamed  sit with your wife or your husband or  your girlfriend or your boyfriend and  say together let's go talk to somebody  do these four things and you will begin  to fireproof your life and one day in  the near future you'll wake up and  you'll realize the alarms have stopped  that you've regained control of your  thoughts and your actions and your life  is on a different trajectory and it's a  trajectory of peace and of joy and a  feeling of lightness that you can't  understand until you experience it for  yourself you can do it and I'm here to  walk alongside you this is John dallona  with Ramsey Network subscribe to all the  things change your thoughts change your  actions and you will change your life  you can do this talk to you soon
 

